<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Data Quality Assessment — {{ filename }}</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 18mm 16mm 20mm 16mm;
    @bottom-center { content: "Data Quality Assessment · " counter(page) " of " counter(pages);
      font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; color: #7A858E; } }
  body { font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #24303A; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.45; }
  h1 { font-size: 22pt; margin: 0 0 4pt; }
  h2 { font-size: 13pt; margin: 22pt 0 6pt; padding-bottom: 4pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8DEE4; }
  h3 { font-size: 11pt; margin: 14pt 0 4pt; }
  .sub { color: #5A6572; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0 0 18pt; }
  .cover { border-left: 4px solid #3D6B54; padding-left: 14pt; margin-bottom: 20pt; }
  .kpis { display: table; width: 100%; margin: 14pt 0; border-spacing: 6pt 0; }
  .kpi { display: table-cell; width: 25%; background: #F4F6F8; padding: 10pt; border-radius: 4pt; }
  .kpi .v { font-size: 17pt; font-weight: bold; display: block; }
  .kpi .l { font-size: 8pt; color: #5A6572; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .score-big { font-size: 40pt; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8pt 0 14pt; font-size: 9pt; }
  th { text-align: left; background: #F4F6F8; padding: 5pt 7pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8DEE4; font-size: 8pt;
       text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; color: #5A6572; }
  td { padding: 5pt 7pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #EDF0F3; vertical-align: top; }
  td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .healthy { color: #2F7A55; } .needs { color: #B5761F; } .critical { color: #B33A3A; }
  .na { color: #7A858E; font-style: italic; }
  .bar { height: 7pt; background: #EDF0F3; border-radius: 3pt; overflow: hidden; width: 100%; }
  .bar span { display: block; height: 100%; }
  .note { background: #F4F6F8; border-left: 3px solid #9AA7B1; padding: 8pt 10pt; font-size: 9pt;
          color: #4A5560; margin: 12pt 0; }
  .dim { page-break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: 16pt; }
  .ex { font-family: "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace; font-size: 8pt; }
  .page-break { page-break-before: always; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="cover">
  <h1>Data Quality Assessment</h1>
  <p class="sub">{{ filename }} · {{ generated }}</p>
</div>

{% macro cls(b) %}{% if b == 'healthy' %}healthy{% elif b == 'needs attention' %}needs{% elif b == 'critical' %}critical{% else %}na{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro colour(s) %}{% if s >= 90 %}#2F7A55{% elif s >= 70 %}#B5761F{% else %}#B33A3A{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

<h2>Overall result</h2>
<p><span class="score-big {{ cls(overall_band) }}">{{ overall if overall is not none else '—' }}</span>
   <span style="font-size:12pt;color:#5A6572;"> / 100 · {{ overall_band }}</span></p>

<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ "{:,}".format(records) }}</span><span class="l">Records assessed</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ columns }}</span><span class="l">Columns found</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ cdes }}</span><span class="l">Critical data elements</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><span class="v">{{ dimensions | selectattr('score') | list | length }}</span><span class="l">Dimensions scored</span></div>
</div>

{% if sampled %}
<div class="note"><strong>Sampled assessment.</strong> This file contains
{{ "{:,}".format(records) }} records, above the threshold for full processing.
A representative sample of {{ "{:,}".format(sampled_rows) }} records was assessed.
Percentages are representative; absolute counts are not exact.</div>
{% endif %}

{% if parse_warnings %}
<div class="note"><strong>{{ "{:,}".format(parse_warnings) }} rows could not be
parsed</strong> and were excluded. This usually indicates inconsistent column
counts in the export itself.</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>What this means</h2>
{% if ranked %}
{% if any_assessed %}
<p>Every dimension assessed in this file, weakest first, with the business
consequence of leaving it unaddressed. Dimensions that could not be assessed
are listed last with the reason.</p>
{% else %}
<p>No dimension could be scored for this file. The reasons are set out below.</p>
{% endif %}
<table>
  <tr><th>Area</th><th class="num">Score</th><th class="num">Failures</th><th>Consequence if unaddressed</th></tr>
  {% for d in ranked %}
  <tr>
    <td><strong>{{ d.label }}</strong></td>
    {% if d.score is not none %}
    <td class="num {{ cls(d.band) }}">{{ d.score }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(d.failed) }}</td>
    <td>{{ d.impact }}</td>
    {% else %}
    <td class="num na">not assessed</td>
    <td class="num na">&mdash;</td>
    <td class="na">{{ d.not_assessed }}</td>
    {% endif %}
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}
<p>No dimension could be scored for this file.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Scope and method</h2>
<p>Every column was profiled and {{ cdes }} of {{ columns }} were identified as
critical data elements — the fields carrying business meaning, as distinct
from system and audit columns. Assessment rules were applied to those fields
across the dimensions below.</p>
<div class="note">{{ deferred_note }}</div>

{% if is_in_depth and cde_columns %}
<h3>Critical data elements assessed</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th><th class="num">Populated</th><th>Why selected</th></tr>
  {% for c in cde_columns %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ c.name }}</td>
    <td>{{ c.semantic_type | replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
    <td class="num">{% if c.total %}{{ "%.0f%%" | format((c.total - c.nulls - c.blanks) / c.total * 100) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ c.cde_reasons | join('; ') }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2>Results by dimension</h2>
{% for d in dimensions %}
<div class="dim">
  <h3>{{ d.label }}
    {% if d.score is not none %}
      <span class="{{ cls(d.band) }}">— {{ d.score }} / 100</span>
    {% else %}<span class="na">— not assessed</span>{% endif %}
  </h3>
  <p style="color:#5A6572;margin:2pt 0 6pt;">{{ d.blurb }}</p>

  {% if d.not_assessed %}
    <div class="note">{{ d.not_assessed }}</div>
  {% else %}
    <div class="bar"><span style="width:{{ d.score }}%;background:{{ colour(d.score) }};"></span></div>
    <p style="font-size:9pt;color:#5A6572;margin:5pt 0 0;">
      {{ "{:,}".format(d.failed) }} failing values across {{ d.rules | length }} rules.</p>
    {% if is_in_depth and d.rules %}
    <table>
      <tr><th>Rule</th><th>Column</th><th class="num">Pass rate</th><th class="num">Failed</th></tr>
      {% for r in d.rules[:rules_shown] %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ r.rule_name }}</td>
        <td>{{ r.column or 'whole record' }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.1f%%" | format(r.passRate * 100) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(r.failed) }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}

{% if is_in_depth %}
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>Example failing records</h2>
<p style="color:#5A6572;">Drawn directly from the assessed file. Row numbers
refer to lines in the original export.</p>
{% for d in dimensions %}{% for ex in d.examples %}
<h3>{{ d.label }} — {{ ex.rule.rule_name }}</h3>
<table class="ex">
  <tr><th>Row</th><th>Column</th><th>Value</th><th>Issue</th></tr>
  {% for row in ex.rows %}
  <tr><td class="num">{{ row.row }}</td><td>{{ row.column or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.value }}</td><td>{{ row.reason }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<h2>Limitations</h2>
<p>Accuracy is assessed without an external source of truth. It covers
reference-list conformance, cross-field contradiction and statistical
outliers, and cannot confirm that a plausible value is factually correct.
Business rules specific to this organisation were not applied; capturing them
is the next step and typically raises the number of findings.</p>

</body>
</html>
